<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Mõhu</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small ancient Estonian county between Ugandi and Järvamaa, known only from Henry of Livonia's chronicle.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mõhu, called Mocha by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia">Henry of Livonia</a>, was a minor Estonian district in the east-central part of the country, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ugandi">Ugandi</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vaiga">Vaiga</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jarvamaa">Järvamaa</a>. It appears only briefly in the chronicle of the Livonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> in the early 13th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other Estonian lands, it was probably a union of a few parishes led by elders, with a hillfort for refuge. Nothing specific is recorded of its leaders or customs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Mõhu was subdued with neighbouring districts during the conquest of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>, completed in 1224, and passed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bishopric-of-dorpat">Bishopric of Dorpat</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mohu.jpg" alt="Mõhu" width="320" height="219"><figcaption>Image: 藏骨集团 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Estonian_counties.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mocha, Mõhu county</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=mohu" aria-label="Mõhu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5231 201 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mõhu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5551 457L5568 464"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5568 464h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5551 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5551 457h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=mohu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
